module gunbc.rung_drop.floor_cut_behavioural_regression_differential

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.rung_drop { RungDrop, Standing, AuthoredProse, FloorCutBehaviouralRegressionDifferential }

data floor_cut_behavioural_regression_differential: RungDrop = RungDrop {
  identity: "floor_cut_behavioural_regression_differential" as NonEmptyStr,

  subject: "Behavioural regression between a changed target's committed build and its candidate emission, by execution",

  declared: "2026-09-03",

  standing: Standing,

  declaration: AuthoredProse { legacy: FloorCutBehaviouralRegressionDifferential, authored: "**NO REQUIRED LANE RUNS A CHANGED TARGET BOTH AS COMMITTED AND AS FRESHLY EMITTED AND COMPARES THE TWO BEHAVIOURS, AND THIS ROW DECLARES THAT RUNG (2026-09-03).** Split out of `floor_cut`, whose loss sentence names this capability and whose five siblings did not carry it. PREVIOUS RUNG: 2 (mechanically preventable) -- the behavioral-differential path was required and could refuse an old-versus-new target divergence. TEMPORARY RUNG: 1 (mitigatable) -- the instrument exists and is careful work: `v1_compiler.behavioral_receipt_host` `behavioral_differential` runs one generated driver against the tree as committed, installs the emitted candidate over its mirror, REBUILDS, runs the same driver again, restores the mirror, and compares transcripts, refusing outright if the mirror is dirty rather than comparing a leftover candidate against itself. WHAT THE INSTRUMENT DOES AND WHAT CI OMITS ARE TWO FACTS, AND AN EARLIER REVISION OF THIS ROW READ THE SECOND AS THE FIRST (corrected 2026-09-03, bright-ram-778 on gunbc#10154). That revision quoted the instrument's own doc comment -- CI proves the committed mirrors equal what the authority emits and that the emit repeats, it never compiles the candidate, let alone runs it -- and carried it as a claim about the MECHANISM. It is not: the sentence describes what the CURRENT REQUIRED COMPOSITION omits, and `behavioral_differential` compiles and runs the candidate by construction. So this row is an ENROLMENT row and nothing else. WHAT THE MERGE PATH ENFORCES INSTEAD is byte agreement plus generation repeatability -- BYTE IDENTITY, which DESIGN section 7 names explicitly as NOT the goal and explains is actively harmful, since a byte-identical fixed point forces v2 to reproduce the seed's warts to match bytes. The enforced property is the disclaimed one; the claimed one has no required consumer. BOUNDED POPULATION: one capability -- refusal, on the merge path, of a behavioural difference between a target as committed and the same target as emitted from the changed authority. RESTORATION TRIGGER, A CAPABILITY: `behavioral_differential` TOGETHER WITH ITS DISCRIMINATING CONTROLS executing in a REQUIRED lane, SUFFICIENT FOR a merge whose candidate target behaves differently from the committed one being refused, demonstrated by a red on a deliberately divergent candidate and by a green on an unchanged one. The controls are half the trigger: a differential that cannot be shown to go red is `floor_cut_receipt_discriminating_arms`'s subject arriving inside this one. WHAT THIS ROW IS NOT: it is the OLD-TARGET-versus-NEW-TARGET relation. Whether the emitted target agrees with the .dag authority that produced it is a different relation on a different pair, filed separately as `gunbc.guarantee_stall` `authority_target_same_expression_equivalence_stall`, and NEITHER implies the other -- see that row for the counterexample in both directions. It is a STALL and not a drop, which is the point of the separate carrier: nothing lowered it, so it has no previous rung to restore. **`floor_cut` CANNOT RETIRE WHILE THIS ROW STANDS.**" }
}
